function renderReport(raw){const impl=raw.implementations||[],hist=raw.historicalDirectTransactions||[],probes=raw.probes||[];return `# Free Protocol Step3 — unverified runtime analysis\n\n**Classification:** ${raw.classification}\n\n## Scope and safety\n\nPinned Ethereum block **${PIN}** / \`${PIN_HASH}\`. Public read-only chain and explorer retrieval only. Provider URLs, raw signatures, endpoint inventories, environment files, keys, forks, signing, broadcasts, positive-value calls, and transactions were not used or emitted. Step2 raw and manifest are hash-bound in the raw artifact.\n\n## Current implementations\n\n| instance | implementation | runtime bytes | runtime keccak256 | selectors | source | CBOR |\n|---|---|---:|---|---:|---|---|\n${impl.map(x=>`| ${x.id} | \`${x.address}\` | ${x.runtime.bytes} | \`${x.runtime.keccak256}\` | ${x.dispatcherSelectorCount} | unverified | solc ${x.runtime.cbor.solc}; IPFS=${x.runtime.cbor.containsIpfsKey} |`).join("\n")}\n\nExact runtime, creation bytecode, deterministic disassembly, selector-to-entry mappings, bounded CFG opcode counts/body hashes, creation transaction/block/creator, source lookup flags, and printable constants are persisted under \`sources/free-protocol-step3-unverified-runtime\` and in the raw artifact.\n\n## Domain literals and lineage\n\n${impl.map(x=>`- **${x.id}:** \`${x.domainLiteral.literal}\` at byte offset(s) ${x.domainLiteral.offsets.join(", ")||"none"}. ${x.domainLiteral.assessment}.`).join("\n")}\n\nStructural comparisons cover exact Step2 BEVM/Bitlayer runtime addresses and the provider-verified, partially verified a97 historical initial source/runtime. They establish AtomicLock lineage and distinct literals only; **they do not establish source equivalence**. Current source and exact semantics remain unavailable.\n\n## Extra selectors, probes, and history\n\n- \`0x2e1a7d4d\`: \`withdraw(uint256)\` is a deterministic canonical-signature candidate/user-supplied label, not a verified current ABI association.\n- \`0x3f489914\`: the supplied \`updateLockedBalance\` label conflicts with the deterministic \`withdraw(uint8,uint256)\` collision candidate; the deployed name/ABI is **ambiguous**.\n- Zero-value fixed-block probes: ${probes.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.rows.length,0)} total; ${probes.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.rows.filter(y=>y.status==="success").length,0)} success; ${probes.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.rows.filter(y=>y.status==="revert").length,0)} revert; all before/after state digests unchanged=${probes.every(x=>x.stateUnchanged)}.\n- Historical direct extra-selector transactions: ${hist.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.summary.transactions,0)}; successful receipts=${hist.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.summary.success,0)}; reverted receipts=${hist.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.summary.revert,0)}; ERC-20 transfer effects=${hist.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.summary.erc20Transfers,0)}; native internal effects=${hist.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.summary.nativeTransfers,0)}. Raw inputs and signatures are not persisted; input hashes, active implementation intervals, receipt status, and bounded effects are.\n\n## Safe relations\n\n${(raw.safeRelations||[]).map(x=>`- **${x.id}:** ${x.relation} \`${x.safe}\`; getVault equality=${x.getVaultEqualsSafe}; Safe→bridge calls=${x.safeToBridgeCalls.length}. Balances/allowances are fixed-block observations, not proof of unverified current semantics.`).join("\n")}\n\n## Candidate matrix\n\n| candidate | runtimeProperty | confidence | impact | role | next proof |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n${raw.candidates.map(x=>`| ${x.candidate} | ${x.runtimeProperty} | ${x.semanticConfidence} | ${x.deployedImpact} | ${x.roleRequired} | ${x.nextProof} |`).join("\n")}\n\n## Gates and blockers\n\nRoute, execution, replay, vulnerability-promotion, and loss gates remain closed. Blockers: no verified/current source; no exact ABI for extra selectors; bounded static CFG cannot prove all dynamic jumps; no positive asset movement was simulated; no loss, unauthorized execution, or replay was proven.\n`}
function renderHandoff(raw){const tx=(raw.historicalDirectTransactions||[]).reduce((n,x)=>n+x.summary.transactions,0),effects=(raw.historicalDirectTransactions||[]).reduce((n,x)=>n+x.summary.erc20Transfers+x.summary.nativeTransfers,0),p=(raw.probes||[]).reduce((n,x)=>n+x.rows.length,0);return `# Coordinator handoff — Free Protocol Step3\n\n- Classification: ${raw.classification}\n- Pin: Ethereum ${PIN}, ${PIN_HASH}\n- Implementations: ${(raw.implementations||[]).length}; selectors: ${(raw.implementations||[]).reduce((n,x)=>n+x.dispatcherSelectorCount,0)}; probes: ${p}; historical extra-selector txs: ${tx}; transfer effects: ${effects}.\n- Runtime hashes: ${(raw.implementations||[]).map(x=>`${x.id}=${x.runtime.keccak256}`).join(", ")}\n- Current source remains unverified. Domain literals and AtomicLock lineage are structural evidence, never source equivalence.\n- Safe/vault relations and balances/allowances are fixed-block observations; authority and exact semantics are not inferred.\n- Route/execution/replay/promotion/loss gates remain closed.\n- Blockers: verified current source/ABI; full dynamic-jump dataflow; exact digest and accounting semantics; positive loss/replay proof.\n- Detached hashes are in \`reports/raw/fast/free-protocol-unverified-runtime.manifest.json\`. No coordinator state was edited.\n`}
